    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d709">

                <pb facs="0856" n="712" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg712"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.05/180: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-12T13:00:00+08:00">November 12, 1929—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 12—9:03 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>983. Acting upon your No. 360, November 2, I have named Jacobs and Bucknell as
                    delegates of the Legation for the negotiations in regard to the Provisional
                    Court.</p>
                <pb facs="0857" n="713" xml:id="pg713"/>
                <p>2. I am preparing to send Bucknell November 14th to Shanghai for consultation
                    with Cunningham and Jacobs and request your approval therefor.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d709-f1"/></p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d709-f1" n="3" xml:id="d709-f1-content">
                <p>The Acting Secretary, in telegram No. 374, November 13, replied, “Your action
                    approved.” (893.05/180)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
